course: dictionary
lesson: 7451
title: Hair words and the clues around them
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A ponytail is a hairstyle. Long hair is pulled back and tied with a band at the back of the head, so it hangs down like a pony's tail. The word joins two smaller words, pony and tail, which is a clue to its meaning.
explain: Read the words around a new word to learn more. In «Lily tells her friends she does not find the ponytail tugging cute — she finds it annoying», the word cute is a clue: the tugging is not nice. Annoying tells you how Lily feels about it.
explain: Phrases help too. «A high ponytail» is tied near the top of the head, and «a low ponytail» is tied lower down. «Tie your hair back in a ponytail» tells you what to do with long hair.
explain: Always check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. Does «a swinging ponytail» still make sense if you read ponytail as hair tied back and hanging down? Yes, so your meaning fits.
fact: A ponytail is long hair pulled back and tied at the back of the head.
fact: A ponytail hangs down like a pony's tail, which is why it has that name.
fact: Schools often ask for long hair to be tied back in a ponytail for PE, science practicals near flames, and swimming, to keep everyone safe.
fact: «A high ponytail» is tied near the top of the head; «a low ponytail» is tied lower down.
fact: A hair tie, or scrunchie, is the band you use to tie a ponytail.
exercise: «Chloe's first drama club, a girl with a ponytail says loudly "Ugh, newbie"» What does ponytail mean? | *A hairstyle with long hair tied back at the back of the head | A band of flowers for the hair | A tail a pony uses to swat flies | A hat worn for swimming
exercise: Schools ask for long hair to be tied back in a ponytail for science practicals near flames. Why? | *To keep hair safe and out of the way | To keep hair dry in the rain | To show you belong to a club | To make the hair look curly
exercise: «Lily tells her friends she does not find the ponytail tugging cute — she finds it annoying.» Find and copy the word that tells you how Lily feels. | tells | cute | *annoying | friends
exercise: In stories, a swinging ponytail often shows what? | *Movement or energy | Being very old | Deep sleep | Heavy rain
exercise: What does «a low ponytail» mean? | Hair that has been shaved off | *Hair tied lower down, near the neck | Hair tied at the very top of the head | Hair cut very short
exercise: In stories, pulling someone's ponytail is a picture of what? | Cooking | Helping them | *Teasing | Sleeping
test: What is a scrunchie? | A small brush for cleaning teeth | *A soft fabric hair band used to tie hair | A fabric hair band used to tie hair | A bright hat for the sun
test: «When a boy kept pulling Lily's ponytail, she walked to the other side of the playground.» What does kept mean here? | Stopped suddenly | Fell over | Pulled just once | *Went on again and again
exam: Which best describes a ponytail? | A type of pony that lives on a farm | Hair that is cut very short at the sides | *Long hair pulled back and tied at the back of the head, hanging down | A hat with a long tail of cloth
